OL,3,GNEWSACrime falls to lowest recorded    
OL,4,Alevel but sexual offences up, figures  
OL,5,Ashow                                   
OL,7,FNew official data suggests that        
OL,8,Frecorded crime in Northern Ireland has 
OL,9,Ffallen to its lowest level since       
OL,10,Fcurrent records began in 1998.         
OL,12,FJust under 94,000 offences were        
OL,13,Frecorded last year, compared to a peak 
OL,14,Fof 138,000 in 2002.                    
OL,16,FIn 2025 there were 49 crimes recorded  
OL,17,Fper 1,000 people, compared with to the 
OL,18,Fpeak of 81 crimes per 1,000 in 2002/03.
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
